nged mapping independently; do not change method/protocol or claim trial readiness.'}, {'id': 'F2', 'category': 'Spec', 'severity': 'high', 'locator': 'benchmark/writing/wp1-key-0115.json#/required_ids (WP1-original-output-grounding), #/rules (R-mapping,R-dimensions)', 'evidence': 'The source-map ID has dimension answer and requires complete original/output support, while R-dimensions/L36 separate correctness from wrong-citation grounding. C1-wrong-existing-citation preserves correct delta text but replaces its source locator with existing, non-supporting Bld_version.major at line 43. Grounding must be incorrect, but the key leaves correctness of its source-map answer ID unspecified: an adjudicator can retain factual correctness or fail that answer ID for deficient support. The frozen atom-to-ID rules do not decide between those assessments.', 'impact': 'A required C1 challenge lacks one unambiguous answer-correctness grade for a new human adjudicator; WP1-original-output-grounding and the affected mapping/dimension rules remain blocked.', 'smallest_correction': 'Freeze separate correctness propositions and grounding tests for each answer ID, explicitly resolve the source-map ID interaction without merging the dimensions, and provide the wrong-existing-citation case with one prescribed item ledger and dimension assessment for independent recheck.'}, {'id': 'P1', 'category': 'Review-process limitation, not a defect attributed to the key', 'severity': 'high', 'locator': '.session/issue.md Acceptance 2; supplied continuation Read wp1-key-0115.md before the original/request derivation', 'evidence': 'The supplied actual-operation continuation reads the markdown key and its expected delta/hash before reading the original and before the first byte/hash calculation; it queries key precondition/delta/prompt before querying the WP1 task request. Later source-only recalculation reproduces 3347/L42/5806/8d984c2e...0e42 but cannot undo this exposure.', 'impact': 'The required bl